# Cached line coverage, written by hk's `coverage` step in fix mode.
#
# WHY A CACHE: measuring costs a full instrumented test run, which is why
# coverage lives in the pre-push set and not in pre-commit. The README badge
# has to be regenerated on every commit, though, so it reads this instead of
# measuring. `readme-badges` is cheap because this file exists.
#
# key is a git SHA over the files that can move coverage -- every tracked
# `*.rs` plus SPEC.md and .spec-records, which tests/dogfood.rs reads:
#
#   git ls-files -s -- '*.rs' SPEC.md .spec-records | git hash-object --stdin
#
# If the key still matches, the number below is current by construction and
# no measurement is needed. If it does not, the cache is stale and pre-push
# says so rather than trusting it.
